Kaiwa uses the following third-party works (ADR-007). Models are downloaded by the
user and are not part of the repository or the program.

- Kokoro-82M v1.0 (hexgrad), Apache-2.0: the interim voice (downloaded).
  ONNX export and voices from kokoro-onnx (thewh1teagle), MIT.
- ReazonSpeech zipformer (Reazon Holdings, via sherpa-onnx), Apache-2.0: speech
  recognition (downloaded).
- kaiwa-kana-ctc (the Kaiwa authors), Apache-2.0: the mora check (downloaded from
  huggingface.co/shrippen/kaiwa-kana-ctc). Fine-tuned from japanese-wav2vec2-large
  (Reazon Holdings), Apache-2.0, on Common Voice 19.0 Japanese (Mozilla), CC0.
- sherpa-onnx (k2-fsa), Apache-2.0, with ONNX Runtime (Microsoft), MIT: linked in.
- misaki (hexgrad), Apache-2.0, and cutlet (Paul O'Leary McCann), MIT: the kana to
  phoneme table and rules in crates/kaiwa-speech/src/g2p are derived from them.
- kaiwa-data (github.com/shrippen/kaiwa-data), CC BY-SA 4.0: the dictionary for the
  word lookup (downloaded, never part of the program). It is derived from JMdict and
  KANJIDIC2, property of the Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group
  (EDRDG), used in conformance with the Group's licence
  (https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html), and from the Kanjium pitch accent data
  by Uros Ozvatic (github.com/mifunetoshiro/kanjium), CC BY-SA 4.0. The excerpt in
  data/dict (demo and tests, not part of the program) is a copy of rows of the same
  package under the same licence, see data/dict/README.md.
- mecab-ipadic-2.7.0-20070801 (NAIST), compiled into the program through lindera
  (MIT). Its notice follows.

